# What the image is NOT built from.
#
# Measured, not guessed: `docker build` streams the WHOLE directory to the daemon
# before it reads the first instruction, so anything left in here is paid on
# every build — and it was being paid. The context was 231MB, almost all of it
# `.venv`, which the image never touches: the Dockerfile installs from
# `pyproject.toml` into its own environment, and a host venv full of
# macOS-compiled wheels would be useless inside Linux even if it were copied.
#
# THE RULE for editing this file: open the Dockerfile and read the `COPY` lines
# first. Everything they name must stay reachable; everything else is weight.
# What this image copies:
#   pyproject.toml · README.md · app/ · web/   ← web/ IS the PWA, not an accessory

# ── the big one ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── build and test leavings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ── history and working notes, which no image needs ──────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/

# ── this repo's own weight ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
tests/
*.sh
.DS_Store
# What a LOCAL run recorded. The image ships no study, and in the stack this path
# is a volume — a container's own data must not be baked into the picture of it.
data/
